# cmd.exe seeks through a batch file as it runs. With LF-only endings that seek
# can land mid-line and break `goto` into the labels the error paths depend on.
#
# `-text` (not `text eol=crlf`) on purpose: `text eol=crlf` stores the blob
# normalised to LF and converts on checkout, which leaves the CRLF depending on
# whoever generates the download. `-text` disables conversion entirely, so the
# exact CRLF bytes are what is stored and what every delivery path hands over:
# a clone, a raw file download, and GitHub's Download ZIP alike.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# Shell scripts must stay LF, even when cloned on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf
